  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Scale-up of Rapid Response for Peace: Immediate Protection and Early Warning Support to Violence-Affected Communities in Benue and Nasarawa States, Nigeria.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: Scale-up of Rapid Response for Peace: Immediate Protection and Early Warning Support to Violence-Affected Communities in Benue and Nasarawa States, Nigeria. - This action will promote stabilisation and peaceful co-existence in Nigeria&#xbf;s Middle Belt. It aims at reducing violence and tensions while reinforcing community resilience and cohesion. The measure will, specifically, strengthen the capacity of local peace infrastructures and religious leaders to prevent and mitigate conflict, including those amplified by mis- and dis-information and identity-based narratives, and it will enhance timely and coordinated interfaith response to emerging violence, limiting escalation and preventing reprisals. Furthermore, it will strengthen social cohesion and trauma management in affected communities, with a focus on women, youth and vulnerable groups.</narrative>
  </description>
